 { Two main weapons in the fight against a fortress are zugzwang and sacrifices. We saw good proof of their use in Matanovic-Larsen and Goldin-Korzubov, and here is another one.With precise play White can take this fortress. } 1. { -KEY- } Rb3 Kf8 2. Re3 Nh7 3. Kd7 Ng5 4. Kd8 Kg7 ( { Black has to let the enemy king come closer, since } 4... Nh7 { would just worsen things after } 5. Re8 Kg7 6. Ke7 Ng5 7. Rf8 $1 { (zugzwang) } Nxh3 8. Rxf7 { and White wins - Finkel. } ) 
5. Ke7 Nh7 6. Ra3 Ng5 7. Rc3 $1 { Losing a tempo. } ( 7. Ra6 $6 Nxh3 8. Rxf6 Ng5 { is less convincing. } ) 
Nh7 ( { On } 7... Ne4 { there follows the same reply. } ) 
8. Rc6 { Black is finally in zugzwang. } Ng5 ( { Or } 8... Kg8 9. Rxf6 $1 Nxf6 10. Kxf6 { with an easy win. } ) 
9. Rxf6 Nxh3 10. Rxf7+ Kh6 11. Rf6+ Kh7 12. Rg6 Nf4 13. Kf7 $1 
 1-0

