Ke3 12. Rf3 Ke2 13. Rf7 Qc5 14. Rf3 Qe7 ( { here and later, } 14... g4 15. Rf4 { when the safe square on f3 is replaced with f4; } ) 
15. Kg1 $1 Qa7 16. Kh2 { and as far as I can see, Black is unable to progress. By the way, note that White's extra pawn rules out a queen sacrifice for the rook; e.g. 9...Qxf4! would have been winning were it not for the g2-pawn. } ) 
